                <pb facs="0375" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7071: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Legation in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-18T14:00:00+08:00">June 18, 1935—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>168. I understand that Executive Yuan this morning approved appointment of Chin
                    Teh-chun, member of Chahar Provincial Government, to be chairman thereof in
                    place of Sung Cheh-yuan. Chin is said to be acceptable to Japanese.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
